From 5e1b1063cf9a4a4b9d4b3861e39faf447b12d370 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moWerk <mo@mowerk.net>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:24:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/16] sfos-venus

SailfishOS build only (applied after sfos-dt): Venus video codec (AR50LT) on SM6115,
for hardware H.264 encode in the camera app (GStreamer v4l2h264enc).

Backport of Dmitry Baryshkov's "media: iris: bring up driver on SM6115-based platforms"
v2 (2026-05): the gcc HW_CTRL_TRIGGER flag for the vcodec0 GDSC and the sm6115 venus
node (DT patches applied by Bjorn Andersson on 2026-07-08), plus the board enable.
The board uses linux-firmware's qcom/venus-6.0/venus.mbn
(6.0-00055): the Fxtec vendor image is 6.0-00049, which the driver rejects (min 6.0.55).
The qcm2290-venus fallback compatible binds the 7.1 venus driver (HFI gen1); iris in 7.1
does not claim AR50LT.


On v7.3 only the board enable remains: the sm6115 venus node and the gcc
HW_CTRL_TRIGGER flag are upstream.

LLMGD-0 A0
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
index b29c33e07..91acd4929 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
@@ -1541,3 +1541,12 @@ camss_csiphy2_ep: endpoint {
 		};
 	};
 };
+
+&venus {
+	/*
+	 * No firmware-name: the Fxtec image (VIDEO.VE.6.0-00049) is older than the 6.0.55
+	 * the driver requires for QCM2290 (encoder needs >= 6.0.54); the driver default
+	 * qcom/venus-6.0/venus.mbn from linux-firmware (6.0-00055) loads on this device.
+	 */
+	status = "okay";
+};
